📖 What is a File?
Definition

A file is a named collection of related information stored on secondary storage.

Easy Definition

A file is simply:

A container that stores data.

Examples:

📄 Resume.pdf

🎵 Song.mp3

🎥 Movie.mp4

🖼️ Photo.jpg

💻 Program.exe

📊 Data.xlsx

🏠 Real-Life Analogy

Imagine:

Cupboard

contains:

Math Notebook
Physics Notebook
Chemistry Notebook

Each notebook stores information.

Similarly:

SSD/HDD

contains:

Resume.pdf
Photo.jpg
Movie.mp4
Why Do We Need Files?

Imagine no files existed.

Every shutdown:

All data disappears.

😱

Example:

You create:

Project Report

Shutdown laptop.

Next day:

Gone forever.

Files provide:

✅ Permanent Storage

✅ Organization

✅ Easy Retrieval

