📋 File Attributes

Every file has metadata.

Metadata means:

Data about Data

Example:

Resume.pdf

contains content.

But OS also stores:

Size
Owner
Creation Date
Permissions
Location
Important File Attributes
1. Name

Example:

Resume.pdf
2. Identifier

Unique ID internally.

Example:

File ID = 7845
3. Size

Example:

5 MB
4. Location

Where file exists on disk.

5. Owner

Who created file.

6. Protection

Who can:

Read
Write
Execute
7. Time Stamps

Stores:

Created Time
Modified Time
Access Time
